"Supplying Eldrin Power": {
  "index": -96,
  "category": "eldrin_altar",
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "title",
      "value": "Supplying Eldrin Power"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "json": [
        {
          "text": "Once I've generated "
        },
        {
          "text": "Eldrin Power",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": " by using Eldrin Fume Filters to burn motes or sachets, I can then "
        },
        {
          "text": "use Eldrin Conduits to supply that eldrin power to things that need",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": " it by bringing that energy back into the material plane. Each conduit can bring forth a different energy.\n\nLesser conduits do not transfer power nearly as quickly, and have a smaller internal storage buffer.  I'll either need to upgrade them to greater conduits, or place multiple conduits down to meet demand."
        },
        {
          "text": "\n\nConduits also have a "
        },
        {
          "text": "range and charge rate",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": " which determines how far they can supply eldrin power and how fast they pull eldrin power into their internal buffer.  Conduits may become over-taxed, meaning they cannot meet demand.  This will not damage the conduit, however, just slow down whatever they are powering.  They can also be shut down by a redstone signal of any strength, which will prevent them from supplying power entirely."
        },
        {
          "text": "\n\nI can see all of this as well as change who can use a conduit by activating it."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
